<title>UK: Freddie Mac prices $800 mln 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac prices $800 mln 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by joint lead managers Goldman Sachs and J.P. Morgan, has now been priced and increased by $50 million to $800 million.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FEDERAL HOME LOAN MORTGAGE CORP</p>
<p> AMT    $800 MLN	COUPON     7.10 PCT  MATURITY    10.APR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.887    PAY DATE    10.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  32.5 BP   REOFFER    99.887    SPREAD	+22 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10+5 MULT SALE LIMITS ***</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   +++</p>
<p> MGT/UND    12.5 BP   SELL CONC  20 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 10-YEAR U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>NOTES  *** UK/JP/FR/DE/HK/SI/TW NOT US</p>
<p>+++ FORM W8 REQUIRED, NO GROSS UP</p>
<p>	  EXEMPT FROM SECURITIES ACT REGISTRATION REQUIREMENTS</p>
<p>	  ISSUED UNDER GLOBAL DEBT FACILITY, BOOK-ENTRY FORM</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
